From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libc: sigaction reports signal 32 at its default

apklayer patch (docs/PATCHES.md). glibc keeps signal 32 (SIGCANCEL) for itself
and its sigaction fails with EINVAL; the kernel, and so bionic, reports it at
SIG_DFL. AOSP's posix_spawn child (ApplyAttrs) queries every signal and exits
127 when one query fails: under the native bridge, whose host sigaction is
bionic_sigaction, every guest system() and every posix_spawn child exited 127
before its exec. A query, or a reset to SIG_DFL, of 32 now succeeds.

--- a/libc/libc.c
+++ b/libc/libc.c
@@ -483,6 +483,14 @@
 {
 	verbose("%d, %p, %p", sig, (void *)act, (void *)oact);
 
+	/* apklayer patch (0070): glibc keeps 32 (SIGCANCEL) and its sigaction refuses it; the kernel (bionic) reports it at its default.
+	 * bionic's posix_spawn child queries every signal and exits 127 on a refusal (translated guests' system and posix_spawn) */
+	if (sig == 32 && (!act || act->bsa_handler == SIG_DFL)) {
+		if (oact)
+			*oact = (struct bionic_sigaction){0};
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	// THREAD_SIGNAL on android used by libbacktrace
 	if (sig == 33)
 		sig = SIGRTMIN;
